    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and all its cases pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added an optional `postcode` field to owners, validated by region when present, with minimal structural impact. Changes:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `postcode` (4-digit) property to the `OwnerFields` schema, so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` (input) and `OwnerDto` (output) both carry it. Not added to `required`, keeping the contract backward-compatible.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `postcode` column field plus a plain getter/setter (two CC-1 methods; no existing method touched). MapStruct maps it automatically by name in both directions, so `BuildOwner`/`ApplyOwner`/the mapper needed no edits.\n\n3. **`ValidatePostcode.java`** (new, cohesive, zero surrounding complexity) \u2014 the only new behaviour: returns immediately when postcode is absent; otherwise requires 4 digits and, when the city's region is known (via the existing `Locality` table), enforces NSW 2000-2099 / VIC 3000-3099 / QLD 4000-4099; unknown regions accept any 4-digit value. A bad postcode is a 400 via the existing `MissingFieldsException` channel (reused rather than adding a new exception + handler + escalation YAML).\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `validatePostcode` step right after field validation.\n\n5. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql` + `db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 added the `postcode` column and the matching value to the 10 positional seed inserts (the test profile is `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`). I deliberately did **not** touch the `h2`/`postgres`/`mysql` schema files \u2014 the default `h2` profile uses `ddl-auto=update` (Hibernate adds the column, and its 10-column `data.sql` inserts stay valid), and touching the others would only have half-migrated them.\n\nTest results: `Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 valid postcode stored and returned, owner without postcode still accepted, malformed postcode rejected with 400.",
